  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Open Rummy. 4-6p partnerships. 3-4 decks. Sequences: 3+ consecutive, max 3 jokers. Groups: 3+ Aces or 3+ Threes only. Draw from discard = play one. Show: 5 complete sets, 1 pure. Target 1500.',
    Player: 'Open Rummy: Partners sit alternately. Draw one from stock or take from discard (must play one). Sequences need 1 natural, max 3 jokers. Only Aces and Threes form groups. Show needs 5 complete sets, 1 pure. First to 1,500 wins.',
    objective: 'First team to reach 1,500 points (4-deck standard). Score from cards on table, opponent unplayed cards, complete-set bonuses, suited-group bonuses, and show bonus.',
    gameplay: '1. Turn order: discard (compulsory) â†’ play combinations (optional) â†’ draw (compulsory). 2. Draw: one from closed pile OR any number from discard pile (if at least one drawn card is immediately played). 3. Combinations: sequences (3+ consecutive same suit; max 3 jokers, min 1 natural); groups of 3+ Threes or 3+ Aces (no jokers). 4. Printed jokers can be replaced by natural cards and reused; sliding jokers (Twos) stay in sequence when replaced, slid to one end. 5. To declare show: team must have 5+ complete sets, at least one pure (no jokers). Wrong show = 0 for declaring team. 6. Ground show: when draw pile empties, player may declare or draw from discard and play one turn.',
    keyRules: [
      'Only Aces and Threes form equal-card groups.',
      'Sequences: max 3 jokers, min 1 natural per sequence.',
      'Taking from discard: must play at least one drawn card immediately.',
      'Show requires 5 complete sets (12 cards 3-A per suit), 1 pure.',
      'Partners cannot share meld area; each player has own area.',
